## Correct Pipeline Execution Patterns

### ✅ CORRECT: Direct execution in terminal
```powershell
$env:PYTHONUNBUFFERED = "1"
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -u scripts/run_full_pipeline.py --no-progress
```

### ✅ CORRECT: Background execution (use this for long-running pipelines)
```powershell
$env:PYTHONUNBUFFERED = "1"
Start-Process -FilePath ".\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" `
  -ArgumentList "-u", "scripts/run_full_pipeline.py", "--no-progress" `
  -RedirectStandardOutput "logs\pipeline.log" `
  -RedirectStandardError "logs\pipeline_err.log" `
  -NoNewWindow
```

### ✅ CORRECT: Dry-run test (3 coins, 1 chunk, 2 folds)
```powershell
$env:PYTHONUNBUFFERED = "1"
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -u scripts/run_full_pipeline.py --no-progress --dry-run
```

### ❌ WRONG: Using bare `python`
```powershell
# NEVER DO THIS
python -u scripts/run_full_pipeline.py --no-progress
# ERROR: No module named 'ggTrader' (venv not active)
```

### ❌ WRONG: Trying to activate venv in same command
```powershell
# NEVER DO THIS
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1; python -u scripts/run_full_pipeline.py --no-progress
# ERROR: Activation script runs but doesn't propagate to next command
```

### ❌ WRONG: Using forward slashes or unquoted paths
```powershell
# NEVER DO THIS
.\\.venv/Scripts/python.exe -u scripts/run_full_pipeline.py
# or
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -u "C:\Users\Name\My Documents\script.py"  # Unquoted = fails
```

