## PowerShell Syntax Rules (MANDATORY)

**Command Chaining**
- ✅ RIGHT: `Cmd1; Cmd2` (semicolon for sequential)
- ❌ WRONG: `Cmd1 && Cmd2` (bash syntax, doesn't work in PowerShell)
- ❌ WRONG: `Cmd1 | head -50` (Unix pipe filter, use `Select-Object -First 50`)

**Piping & Filtering**
- ✅ RIGHT: `$output = cmd 2>&1; $output | Select-String "error"`
- ✅ RIGHT: `cmd 2>&1 | Select-Object -First 100` (show first 100 lines)
- ✅ RIGHT: `cmd | Select-Object -Last 50` (show last 50 lines)
- ❌ WRONG: `cmd | grep "error"` (Unix tool, not available in PowerShell)
- ❌ WRONG: `cmd | head -50` (Unix tool, not available in PowerShell)

**File Operations**
- ✅ RIGHT: `Get-ChildItem "C:\path" -Recurse`
- ✅ RIGHT: `Get-Content "C:\path\file.txt" -Tail 50`
- ✅ RIGHT: `Test-Path "C:\path" -PathType Container`
- ❌ WRONG: `ls -la /path` (Unix syntax)
- ❌ WRONG: `cat file.txt` (Unix tool)

**Sleep/Wait**
- ✅ RIGHT: `Start-Sleep -Seconds 5`
- ❌ WRONG: `sleep 5` (Unix command)

**Output Redirection**
- ✅ RIGHT: `python script.py 2>&1` (redirect stderr to stdout)
- ✅ RIGHT: `python script.py *>&1` (redirect all to stdout)
- ❌ WRONG: `python script.py 2>&1 | head -50` (head is Unix tool)

