## Monitoring a Running Pipeline

**Option 1: Real-time status with auto-refresh (RECOMMENDED)**
```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/pipeline_status.py --watch
```

**Option 2: Stream status file with updates**
```powershell
Get-Content "results\pipeline_*\status.txt" -Wait -Tail 30
```

**Option 3: Check if running + show status**
```powershell
$proc = Get-Process python -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.CommandLine -like "*run_full_pipeline*" }
if ($proc) { 
    "✓ Pipeline is running (PID $($proc.Id))"
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/pipeline_status.py
} else { 
    "✗ Pipeline is not running"
}
```

**Option 4: Continuous monitor (updates every 10 seconds)**
```powershell
while ($true) {
    Clear-Host
    Get-ChildItem "results" -Directory | Sort-Object CreationTime -Descending | Select-Object -First 1 | ForEach-Object {
        Get-Content "$($_.FullName)\status.txt" -Tail 25 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    }
    "--- Last update: $(Get-Date) ---"
    Start-Sleep -Seconds 10
}
```

